From: OpenX6X00 <noreply@rf.guru>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: rtw88: TX report with long timeout for non-PCIE devices

lwfinger/rtw88 4f88655 ("increase TX report timeout to fix race
condition", Cc: stable) and c141bdd ("TX report with long timeout for
non-PCIE devices", Cc: stable) together, on the 461b696 pin of the X6200
buildroot tree: USB and SDIO chips (the X6200's RTL8723DU) often report TX
status later than 500 ms; the purge timer then dropped the frames and
mac80211 counted them lost ("failed to get tx report from firmware"),
which also hits authentication and association frames.

Upstream authors: Luka Gejak <luka.gejak@linux.dev>,
Ping-Ke Shih <pkshih@realtek.com>.
---
--- a/tx.c
+++ b/tx.c
@@ -219,6 +219,7 @@
 void rtw_tx_report_enqueue(struct rtw_dev *rtwdev, struct sk_buff *skb, u8 sn)
 {
 	struct rtw_tx_report *tx_report = &rtwdev->tx_report;
+	unsigned long timeout;
 	unsigned long flags;
 	u8 *drv_data;
 
@@ -230,7 +231,12 @@
 	__skb_queue_tail(&tx_report->queue, skb);
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&tx_report->q_lock, flags);
 
-	mod_timer(&tx_report->purge_timer, jiffies + RTW_TX_PROBE_TIMEOUT);
+	if (rtwdev->hci.type == RTW_HCI_TYPE_PCIE)
+		timeout = RTW_TX_PROBE_TIMEOUT_SHORT;
+	else
+		timeout = RTW_TX_PROBE_TIMEOUT_LONG;
+
+	mod_timer(&tx_report->purge_timer, jiffies + timeout);
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(rtw_tx_report_enqueue);
 
--- a/tx.h
+++ b/tx.h
@@ -7,7 +7,8 @@
 
 #define RTK_TX_MAX_AGG_NUM_MASK		0x1f
 
-#define RTW_TX_PROBE_TIMEOUT		msecs_to_jiffies(500)
+#define RTW_TX_PROBE_TIMEOUT_SHORT	msecs_to_jiffies(500)
+#define RTW_TX_PROBE_TIMEOUT_LONG	msecs_to_jiffies(2500)
 
 struct rtw_tx_desc {
 	__le32 w0;
